<section class="tw-hero"><div class="tw-w"><div class="tw-hero-t"><p class="tw-chip">Fibres &middot; Sizes &middot; Care</p><h1>Socks, sorted.</h1><p class="tw-lead">Toewear is a friendly, independent guide to the most overlooked thing you wear. Find your true size, the right fibre for your day and the height that suits your shoes.</p><p class="tw-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Try the sock tools</a><a class="btn tw-ghost" href="sock-fibre-guide.html">Read the fibre guide</a></p></div>
<div class="tw-hero-p"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794761716287-9d49a9125fad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1100&h=560&q=75" alt="olive sneakers worn with white socks with red hearts" width="1100" height="560" fetchpriority="high"><div class="tw-tag tw-tag1"><b>Merino</b><span>warm, breathable, low odour</span></div><div class="tw-tag tw-tag2"><b>Size M</b><span>fits shoe US 7&ndash;9</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tw-s"><div class="tw-w"><div class="tw-hd2"><h2>A sock for every kind of day</h2><p>Different days need different socks. Here is what to reach for.</p></div><div class="tw-moods">
<article><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794208248749-0373ed5c9ad0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=360&q=75" alt="feet in patterned wool socks by a fireplace" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><div><h3>Cosy evenings</h3><p>Thick wool or a wool-blend lounge sock. Loose cuffs, soft knit, extra warmth.</p></div></article>
<article><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793982661450-d731ac0cc6f1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=360&q=75" alt="white socks worn with green football boots" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><div><h3>Sport and training</h3><p>Synthetic blend with targeted cushioning and a snug arch band that stops slipping.</p></div></article>
<article><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792579289644-77cabae36c74?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=360&q=75" alt="pink hiking boots worn with white socks" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><div><h3>Trail and hiking</h3><p>Merino blend, crew height or taller, with cushioning under heel and toe.</p></div></article></div></div></section>

<section class="tw-tl" id="tools"><div class="tw-w"><div class="tw-hd2"><h2>Three sock tools</h2><p>Pick a tab. Your answer updates as you choose.</p></div>
<div class="tw-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Sock tools"><button role="tab" id="tb-1" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tp-1">Size converter</button><button role="tab" id="tb-2" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tp-2">Fibre finder</button><button role="tab" id="tb-3" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tp-3">Height matcher</button></div>
<div class="tw-panel" role="tabpanel" id="tp-1" aria-labelledby="tb-1"><div class="tw-pg"><div><h3>Sock Size Converter</h3><p>Socks are sold in ranges. Enter your shoe size to find yours.</p><label for="sz-s">Shoe size system<select id="sz-s"><option value="us_m">US men&rsquo;s</option><option value="us_w">US women&rsquo;s</option><option value="uk">UK</option><option value="eu">EU</option></select></label><label for="sz-v">Shoe size<input id="sz-v" type="number" step="0.5" value="9"></label><label for="sz-t">Sock thickness<select id="sz-t"><option value="thin">Thin / dress</option><option value="mid" selected>Everyday</option><option value="thick">Thick / hiking</option></select></label></div><div class="tw-out" id="sz-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div>
<div class="tw-panel" role="tabpanel" id="tp-2" aria-labelledby="tb-2" hidden><div class="tw-pg"><div><h3>Fibre Finder</h3><p>Tell us your day; we suggest a fibre.</p><label for="ff-a">Main activity<select id="ff-a"><option value="office">Office and errands</option><option value="run">Running and gym</option><option value="hike">Hiking</option><option value="lounge">Lounging at home</option><option value="formal">Formal occasions</option></select></label><label for="ff-c">Weather<select id="ff-c"><option value="hot">Hot</option><option value="mild" selected>Mild</option><option value="cold">Cold</option></select></label><label for="ff-s">Feet tend to be<select id="ff-s"><option value="norm">Normal</option><option value="sweat">Sweaty</option><option value="cold">Cold</option><option value="sens">Sensitive skin</option></select></label></div><div class="tw-out" id="ff-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div>
<div class="tw-panel" role="tabpanel" id="tp-3" aria-labelledby="tb-3" hidden><div class="tw-pg"><div><h3>Sock Height Matcher</h3><p>Choose your shoes and how you wear your trousers.</p><label for="hm-s">Shoes<select id="hm-s"><option value="loafer">Loafers or boat shoes</option><option value="trainer">Low trainers</option><option value="hightop">High-top trainers</option><option value="dress">Dress shoes</option><option value="boot">Ankle boots</option><option value="hike">Hiking boots</option></select></label><label for="hm-t">Trousers or legs<select id="hm-t"><option value="long">Full-length trousers</option><option value="crop">Cropped trousers</option><option value="short">Shorts or a skirt</option></select></label></div><div class="tw-out" id="hm-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="tw-s"><div class="tw-w tw-anat"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792768646924-328f1a05b30d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=620&q=75" alt="light green socks worn with black platform shoes" width="560" height="620" loading="lazy"></figure><div><h2>Anatomy of a good sock</h2><p>Turn a sock inside out and you can tell a lot about it.</p><ul class="tw-pins"><li><b>Cuff</b>Ribbed and springy, holds without pinching.</li><li><b>Heel pocket</b>A shaped, Y-heel that cups the heel so the sock does not twist.</li><li><b>Arch band</b>A slightly tighter zone that stops the sock bunching.</li><li><b>Cushioning</b>Terry loops where you need them: heel, ball and toe.</li><li><b>Toe seam</b>Flat, ideally hand-linked, so you cannot feel a ridge.</li></ul></div></div></section>

<section class="tw-s tw-mint"><div class="tw-w"><div class="tw-hd2"><h2>Two guides worth reading</h2></div><div class="tw-gds"><a href="sock-fibre-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794208248711-377c10c3c258?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=380&q=75" alt="patterned wool socks on a blanket" width="640" height="380" loading="lazy"><span class="tw-gl">Guide &middot; 7 min</span><h3>The Sock Fibre Guide</h3><p>Cotton, merino, nylon, bamboo viscose and blends compared, plus how to wash each one.</p></a><a href="sock-sizing-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792762976844-07289d4b4051?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=380&q=75" alt="green sneakers with white socks" width="640" height="380" loading="lazy"><span class="tw-gl">Guide &middot; 6 min</span><h3>The Sock Sizing Guide</h3><p>Size ranges, heights and why the heel pocket matters more than the label.</p></a></div></div></section>

<section class="tw-s"><div class="tw-w tw-care"><div><h2>Sock care in five steps</h2><ol class="tw-steps"><li><span>1</span>Turn socks inside out before washing.</li><li><span>2</span>Wash at 30&deg;C, or cold for wool.</li><li><span>3</span>Skip fabric softener; it clogs moisture-wicking fibres.</li><li><span>4</span>Air dry, or tumble on low for synthetics only.</li><li><span>5</span>Pair and fold, don&rsquo;t ball, so cuffs stay springy.</li></ol></div><div class="tw-faq-w"><h2>Quick questions</h2><div class="tw-faq"><details open><summary>What sock size should I buy?</summary><p>Sock sizes usually cover a range of shoe sizes. Find the range that includes your shoe size; if you sit at the top of a range, the next size up often fits better, especially in thick socks.</p></details><details><summary>Which fibre is best for sweaty feet?</summary><p>Merino wool and synthetic blends move moisture away from skin far better than cotton. For sport, a synthetic or merino blend with a little elastane is a good choice.</p></details><details><summary>Why do my socks slide down?</summary><p>Usually the size is too large, the cuff elastic has worn out, or the sock height does not suit the shoe. A snug heel pocket and a ribbed cuff help socks stay up.</p></details><details><summary>How often should I replace socks?</summary><p>When the heel or toe goes thin, the cushioning flattens or the cuff no longer holds. For socks worn weekly, that is often after around a year.</p></details><details><summary>Can I tumble dry wool socks?</summary><p>It is best not to. Heat and tumbling can shrink and felt wool. Wash inside out on a cool, gentle cycle and dry flat or on a rack.</p></details><details><summary>What are no-show socks for?</summary><p>They sit below the edge of low shoes such as loafers and trainers, so they are hidden but still protect your feet and the shoe lining. A silicone heel grip stops them slipping off.</p></details></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tw-nl"><div class="tw-w"><div class="tw-nl-b"><h2>The Toewear Note</h2><p>A short, friendly email each month: one sock tip, one care myth busted.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@toewear.com?subject=The%20Toewear%20Note&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></div></section>

